<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <IncludeBuildOutput>false</IncludeBuildOutput>
    <GenerateDependencyFile>false</GenerateDependencyFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU5128;NU5100</NoWarn>
    <PackageId>TINS.Native.FFTW.Desktop</PackageId>
    <!-- GPL-2.0-or-later, matching the RID packages this depends on; see CLAUDE.md's decision
         on the FFTW/core license split for why FFTW lives in its own opt-in family at all. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-2.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Description>Meta-package bundling TINS.Native.FFTW.win-x64, TINS.Native.FFTW.linux-x64, and TINS.Native.FFTW.osx-arm64, so a multi-platform consumer that has already decided to accept FFTW's GPL-2.0-or-later obligation can pull in FFTW for every built desktop RID with a single reference instead of adding each RID package individually. A single-RID deployment should still reference just its own TINS.Native.FFTW.&lt;rid&gt; package directly -- this carries no native content of its own. osx-x64 is deliberately excluded (see the PackageReference comment below), unlike the core TINS.Native.Desktop package, which does include a placeholder for it.</Description>
    <PackageTags>Neuroscience, Native, FFTW, GPL, Desktop</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Same floor-pinning rationale as TINS.Native.Desktop (see that project's own comment for the
         full three-iteration history): "0.0.0-alpha.1.22" is the height all three of these RIDs
         were actually built and smoke-tested at (2026-09-23, first CI run of the FFTW/core split).

         osx-x64 is NOT referenced here at all, unlike TINS.Native.Desktop (which does include an
         osx-x64 PackageReference, pinned to a non-functional placeholder left over from before this
         repo had a real build for it). TINS.Native.FFTW.osx-x64 has never been built even as a
         placeholder under this new split naming; no package by that name/version exists in any
         feed today. Referencing it here would make this meta-package fail to restore entirely,
         which is strictly worse than a 3-of-4-RID bundle that actually works. Add it back once
         TINS.Native.FFTW.osx-x64 exists in some form (real build or at least a repacked
         placeholder matching this height), rather than fabricating one just for this file. -->
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.FFTW.win-x64" Version="0.0.0-alpha.1.22" />
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.FFTW.linux-x64" Version="0.0.0-alpha.1.22" />
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.FFTW.osx-arm64" Version="0.0.0-alpha.1.22" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
